# NT_187395.1_regions.bed — Homo sapiens chromosome 22 ALT contig slice 1..3000 bp
# Source: NCBI E-utilities feature table pulled on 2026-07-25:
#   https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/efetch.fcgi
#     ?db=nucleotide&id=NT_187395.1&rettype=ft&retmode=text&seq_start=1&seq_stop=3000
# Local mirror: data/bio/annotations/NT_187395.1_features_first3000.txt
# (GFF3 fetch also attempted at NT_187395.1_full.gff3 — same empty result.)
#
# !! IMPORTANT — empty file is the GENUINE annotation state for this slice. !!
# NT_187395.1 is an ALT (alternate) locus scaffold in GRCh38.p14; the curated
# RefSeq / GENCODE gene models do NOT cover this ALT contig, so the feature
# table comes back with no gene calls. Do NOT fabricate annotations to make
# the per-bin analysis look populated.
#
# Behavioral consequence: when bio_probe.py is run with this annotation file,
# every window will be tagged "intergenic" by the max-overlap classifier
# (no intersecting features). The bin dict will contain a single
# "intergenic" entry covering all windows, and its delta_window_H_mean will
# be computed against the composition-preserving shuffle of the pooled
# intergenic bases. That is the correct, honest signal.
#
# Format: BED4 (0-based, half-open intervals; type ∈ one of our 4 bins).
# (No body rows — there are no annotated features for this slice.)
